abstract: >-
  A browser-based research application for navigating supported optical
  coherence tomography datasets, viewing retinal B-scans, overlaying stored
  retinal-boundary predictions from released cross-device models, and running
  those models on registered custom B-scans.
keywords:
  - optical coherence tomography
  - retinal layer segmentation
  - cross-device generalisation
  - medical image analysis
  - research software
